{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3123","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3123","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3123\",\"parent_revision\":\"9477693bf8ecb25e8b33d24fe2d0d0e2a0979ca077256f52f598ccba00986683\",\"root_revision\":\"9477693bf8ecb25e8b33d24fe2d0d0e2a0979ca077256f52f598ccba00986683\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\ndh:contract-verification (and likely other file-path-consuming dh subagents) resolves a relative file path passed in its delegation prompt against the main checkout instead of the dispatching agent's own worktree. Observed during the #3060 incident investigation: a contract-verification subagent dispatched from a worktree-isolated session, given a relative path, produced a fabricated CONTRACT VIOLATION report matching stale code in the main checkout rather than the worktree's actual (fixed) code \u2014 confirmed by byte-for-byte diff. Impact: any quality-gate review or verification subagent dispatched with a relative path from a worktree context can silently report against the wrong code, undermining trust in that review.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **dh subagents resolve relative file paths against main checkout instead of dispatching agent's worktree** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"22b5e7c60b8f3f374ec2247a89e31c114e761eeef948c9dfdf9beeb0be5935fe\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQIoqkA\"}"}